{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>The second time</b><br>And as you said upon \"until the day breathes\" — therefore I went to the mountain of myrrh for the good fragrance (to you)." "<b>The third time</b><br>The words of the Shekhinah are until \"the day breathes.\" [The meaning:] I sit on Mount Moriah as long as the day does not change. And the matter concerns the deed of the congregation of Israel."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:15.561126755Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}